/*!
\page pscf_rp_page pscf_rp - SCFT and PS-FTS with Periodic Fields

Main program for self-consistent field theory (SCFT) and partial-saddle 
point field-theoretic simulation (PS-FTS) of polymer liquids in a domain 
with periodic boundary conditions, using real fields.

The file pscf_rpc is the executable for version of the program that uses 
standard CPU hardware, while pscf_rpg runs a functionally equivalent version 
that uses an NVIDIA GPU. By default, these executables are both created in 
the bin/ directory of the PSCF repository root directory. The instructions 
given below assume that the users shell command search path includes this
directory.

\section pscf_rpc_usage_section Usage

The command line interfaces for pscf_rpc and pscf_rpg are identical, except
for the use of different executable file names. All options are listed 
below: 

\code
   pscf_rpc -d dimension -p file -c file [-i prefix] [-o prefix] [-e]
\endcode

\code
   pscf_rpg -d dimension -p file -c file [-i prefix] [-o prefix] [-e]
\endcode

\section pscf_rpc_options_section Command Line Options

The -d, -p and -c options are required. The -i, -o, and -e options are 
optional. 

  -d dimension

   Set the spatial dimension (# of periodic coordinates) of the 
   structure of interest, given by the integer argument "dimension", 
   which must equal 1, 2 or 3. For example, set dimension equal to 1
   for a lamellar phase, 2 for a hexagonal phase, and 3 for any fully
   three-dimensional structure. (required)

  -p file

   Set the parameter file name, given by argument "file". (required)

  -c file

   Set the command file name, given by argument "file". (required)

  -i prefix

   Set the input file path prefix, given by argument "prefix". (optional)

  -o prefix

   Set the output file path prefix, given by argument "prefix". (optional)

  -e

   Enable echoing of parameter file to standard output as it is read.
   This option is useful for debugging the parameter file. (optional)

*/
